Size: keep one copy of each typed array's sort.

JSGenericTypedArrayView<Adaptor>::sort() expands std::sort for the element
type. It was inlined into both %TypedArray%.prototype.sort and toSorted, for
all eleven element types, making each of those two functions over 200 KiB.
Out of line, the two callers share one instantiation per type. Sorting a
typed array pays one extra call.

--- a/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/JSGenericTypedArrayView.h
+++ b/Source/JavaScriptCore/runtime/JSGenericTypedArrayView.h
@@ -123,7 +123,7 @@
     static inline std::optional<ElementType> toAdaptorNativeFromValueWithoutCoercion(JSValue);
 
     enum class SortResult { Success, OutOfMemory, Failed };
-    inline SortResult sort();
+    NEVER_INLINE SortResult sort();
 
     inline bool canAccessRangeQuickly(size_t offset, size_t length);
 
